@startuml install-minimal-architecture
title Install Minimal Profile Architecture
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Canonical Python Package" {
  [CLI Doctor]
  [CLI Install]
  [Interactive Session Loop]
  [Install Orchestrator]
  [Install Preflight]
  [Install Planner]
  [Template Locator]
  [Profile Template Resolver]
  [Profile Writer]
  [Install Validator]
  [Rollback Guidance]
  [Install Text Renderer]
  [Install Models]
  [Doctor Orchestrator]
  [Diagnostic Models]
  [Packaged Resources a11y-emacs]
}

database "Project-Owned Profile Directory" as ProfileDir
folder "Development Template Path" as DevPath
folder "Future Frozen Bundle" as FrozenBundle
cloud "Filesystem" as FS
component Emacs

[CLI Install] --> [Install Orchestrator]
[Interactive Session Loop] --> [CLI Install]
[Install Orchestrator] --> [Doctor Orchestrator]
[Install Orchestrator] --> [Install Preflight]
[Install Orchestrator] --> [Install Planner]
[Install Orchestrator] --> [Template Locator]
[Template Locator] --> [Profile Template Resolver]
[Profile Template Resolver] --> [Packaged Resources a11y-emacs]
[Profile Template Resolver] --> [DevPath]
[Profile Template Resolver] --> [FrozenBundle]
[Install Orchestrator] --> [Profile Writer]
[Install Orchestrator] --> [Install Validator]
[Install Orchestrator] --> [Rollback Guidance]
[Install Orchestrator] --> [Install Text Renderer]
[Install Planner] --> [Install Models]
[Profile Writer] --> [FS]
[Profile Writer] --> [ProfileDir]
[Install Validator] --> [FS]
[Install Validator] --> Emacs
[Doctor Orchestrator] --> [Diagnostic Models]

note bottom
Install runs mandatory preflight first.
If Emacs is missing, flow aborts with CRITICAL
before template/planner/writer.
If Emacs is available, flow proceeds to planning,
writing, validation and rollback guidance.
end note
@enduml
